# Songhealth's site configuration for the host's Caddy (Feature 016; production-host-contract.md
# §1). The host's Caddyfile imports this file from a path the host chooses, and defines the two
# snippets it imports, so that no address and no certificate path enters this repository:
#   songhealth_private  who may reach the site before the cutover (spec #450, "Access before the
#                       cutover"): it closes the connection for every other source
#   songhealth_tls      the certificate and key for the site's name, from files the Operator places
# The site answers songhealth.moph.go.th alone; closing every other name is the host's rule, kept
# outside this file. It forwards to the application's loopback publication (production-foundation.md
# §2), passing that name as a fixed Host, so the application never builds a request from a name a
# client sent (#218's first finding). It limits the request body and refuses /_image (below).
# scripts/stack-check.ts checks all of it through the proxy at the site's name. Checked on Caddy
# 2.11.9 from Caddy's official repository (10-system-blueprint.md §3.1 item 8).
songhealth.moph.go.th {
	import songhealth_tls
	# `route` keeps the order written here, where Caddy would otherwise sort the directives
	# (https://caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/route): the source is checked before
	# anything else answers.
	route {
		import songhealth_private
		# 51 MiB: the Admin's largest upload, 50 MiB (EmDash 1.1.0's default `maxUploadSize`,
		# src/api/schemas/media.ts `DEFAULT_MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE`, which astro.config.mjs keeps), with
		# 1 MiB for a multipart form's framing. A larger body is refused before it reaches the
		# application; under it, EmDash's own limits answer.
		request_body {
			max_size 51MiB
		}
		# /_image would make a rendition at any size a request names, and its stock endpoint fetches
		# what the request points at (Astro 7.3.5 astro/dist/assets/endpoint/node.js, which
		# @astrojs/node sets; #218's second finding). Public pages never ask for it in
		# production (ADR 0003). The Admin asks it for thumbnails of the site's own media files: such
		# a request is redirected to that original file, so no rendition is made and the picker's
		# selection tray, which has no fallback of its own, still shows the picture (Product Owner,
		# #458 comment 7209607314). The key is the form EmDash stores, a ULID and the file's
		# extension (EmDash 1.1.0 src/astro/routes/api/media/upload-url.ts `storageKey`). Every other
		# /_image request is refused here. Caddy's path matcher compares the decoded, cleaned path
		# without regard to case (Caddy 2.11.9 modules/caddyhttp/matchers.go `MatchPath`), so the
		# encoded, doubled-slash and dot-segment spellings that reach Astro's endpoint are matched.
		@image_original {
			path /_image*
			expression `{query.href}.matches("^https://songhealth[.]moph[.]go[.]th/_emdash/api/media/file/[A-Za-z0-9_-][A-Za-z0-9._-]*([?]_emdash_media=[A-Za-z0-9%._-]*)?$")`
		}
		redir @image_original {query.href} 302
		@image path /_image*
		respond @image "Songhealth: /_image is refused at the proxy (#218)." 403
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4321 {
			header_up Host songhealth.moph.go.th
		}
	}
	# The body limit's refusal, in EmDash's own error shape, so the Admin shows its message.
	handle_errors 413 {
		header Content-Type "application/json; charset=utf-8"
		respond `{"success":false,"error":{"code":"REQUEST_BODY_TOO_LARGE","message":"คำขอมีขนาดเกิน 51 MiB ที่เว็บไซต์รับได้ (the request body is larger than the site accepts: 51 MiB)"}}` 413
	}
	# While the application is stopped for the night's Recovery Set (#460; spec #450 "Recovery Sets,
	# every night"), reverse_proxy cannot connect and raises a 502 error, which error routes handle;
	# a response the application writes, a 502 included, does not reach them
	# (https://caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/handle_errors and caddyfile/patterns
	# "Reverse proxy"; on Caddy 2.11.9 the rehearsal machine's `stack-check --stopped` read the
	# notice with the application stopped, #460). Every address that reaches the application then
	# answers this static notice with 503. /_image keeps its answers above, and a source outside the
	# allowed network still gets none (Product Owner, #460 comment 7214747287). The notice needs
	# nothing the stopped application serves: no font, picture or script. Its colours are DESIGN.md's
	# surface-soft, text-primary and brand-primary, written out.
	handle_errors 502 {
		header Content-Type "text/html; charset=utf-8"
		header Retry-After 300
		header Cache-Control no-store
		respond <<HTML
		<!doctype html>
		<html lang="th">
		<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8">
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
		<meta name="songhealth-notice" content="nightly-recovery-set">
		<title>สำรองข้อมูลประจำวัน | สำนักงานสาธารณสุขอำเภอสอง</title>
		</head>
		<body style="margin: 0; background: #eaf5f0; color: #16211d; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; line-height: 1.7">
		<main style="max-width: 36rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.25rem">
		<p style="margin: 0; color: #0b6b57; font-weight: 700">สำนักงานสาธารณสุขอำเภอสอง</p>
		<h1 style="margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; font-size: 1.75rem; line-height: 1.4">ขณะนี้เว็บไซต์กำลังสำรองข้อมูลประจำวัน</h1>
		<p style="margin: 0">เว็บไซต์ปิดชั่วคราวเพียงไม่กี่นาที กรุณากลับมาใหม่อีกครั้งในอีกสักครู่</p>
		</main>
		</body>
		</html>
		HTML 503
	}
}
